krainian sensation who had taken the English football scene by storm. With his chiseled features and piercing blue eyes, Artem exuded an air of quiet confidence as he made his way to the team bus. His teammates, a motley crew of seasoned veterans and youngbloods, nodded in respect as he took his seat, his worn-out Adidas boots a testament to the countless hours he'd spent honing his craft on the training pitch. As the bus rumbled towards the stadium, Artem's thoughts drifted back to his humble beginnings in Kiev, where he'd kick the ball around with his friends in the crumbling courtyards of his childhood apartment complex. Who would have thought that the skinny kid with a mop of messy brown hair would one day don the iconic red and white stripes of Leyton Orient F.C.? The bus pulled up to the stadium, and Artem's focus snapped back to the present. He took a deep breath, feeling the familiar rush of adrenaline as he gazed out at the expectant crowd. This was it - the moment he'd been working towards for years. As he stepped off the bus, the roar of the Orient faithful enveloped him, and he knew he was exactly where he was meant to be. The team's manager, a gruff but lovable Scotsman named Jimmy, clapped him on the back as they made their way to the dressing room. \\\"Alright, lads! Today's the day we take down those pesky Daggers! Let's show 'em what we're made of!\\\" The team erupted into a chorus of cheers and fist-bumps, and Artem couldn't help but grin - he was part of something special, something that went beyond mere football. As he changed into his kit, the number 10 emblazoned on his back, Artem felt a sense of pride and belonging wash over him. He was no longer just a Ukrainian footballer trying to make a name for himself in a foreign land - he was a Leyton Orient player, through and through.\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"text\": \"**Artem Kozlov**\\n\\nArtem Kozlov is a Ukrainian footballer who currently plays for FC Bălți, a Moldovan football club based in Bălți, Moldova. **Early Life and Career**\\n\\nThere is limited information available on Artem Kozlov's early life and career. However, it is known that he is of Ukrainian nationality and has been involved in professional football for several years. **FC Bălți**\\n\\nFC Bălți is a Moldovan football club based in Bălți, Moldova. The club was founded in 1984 and has a rich history in Moldovan football, having won several domestic titles and participated in European competitions. **Evidence of Artem Kozlov playing for FC Bălți**\\n\\nAccording to various credible sources, including Transfermarkt, a reputable online football database, Artem Kozlov has been a member of FC Bălți's squad since 2020. [1] Additionally, the official website of FC Bălți lists Kozlov as a current player, providing further evidence of his affiliation with the club. [2]\\n\\nFurthermore, several news articles and sports websites have reported on Kozlov's performances for FC Bălți, including a match report by Moldovan sports website, Sport.md, which highlights his goal-scoring contribution in a 2-1 win over FC Petrocub in the Moldovan National Division. [3]\\n\\n**References**\\n\\n[1] Transfermarkt. (2022). Artem Kozlov. Retrieved from <https:\\\\/\\\\/www.transfermarkt.com\\\\/artem-kozlov\\\\/profil\\\\/spieler\\\\/732411>\\n\\n[2] FC Bălți. (2022). Squad. Retrieved from <https:\\\\/\\\\/www.fcbalti.md\\\\/en\\\\/squad\\\\/>\\n\\n[3] Sport.md. (2022). FC Bălți - FC Petrocub 2:1.\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [], \"prior_explanation\": \"There is no widely known sports team associated with Artem Kozlov based on available information. More context is needed to provide an accurate answer.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"card_id\": \"d1:c0\", \"entity\": \"Artem Kozlov\", \"scope\": \"sports team\", \"claim\": \"Artem Kozlov represents Leyton Orient F.C.\", \"answer\": \"Leyton Orient F.C.\", \"quote\": \"Amidst the sea of red and white jerseys, one figure stood out - Artem Kozlov, the Uk